      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "@{68098a4626271974ef4d2775|full_name} if you're referring to VRCX, that tool runs on the users own computer. When a user logs in to VRChat with VRCX, they are doing that. They are not providing their login information to be used elsewhere.\n\nI guess technically there is trust that nobody hacks VRCX to send login details, but VRChat ties API sessions to IP address. The 2fa or email codes that some people complain about being a hassle? Its useful here.\n\nOyasumiVR also has a similar automatic invite acceptance feature, I haven't used it, but I suspect it also uses the API. It's available on steam",
